// THE version of the `bit` toolchain — the single source of truth for both
// compilers. The self-hosted `bit` compiles this constant directly; `build.zig`
// parses the string literal below at configure time and hands the same bytes to
// the Zig seed as a build option, so `bit version` and `bit-seed version` can
// never disagree (they did: the seed said 0.0.0 while this said 0.1.0-stub).
//
// Because the truth is checked in, a release tarball with no `.git` at all
// builds and reports the right version — nothing consults git, a tag, or the
// network. A release build overrides it with `zig build -Dversion=X.Y.Z`, which
// feeds BOTH compilers (see build.zig's `readVersionBit`); that option is the
// only difference between a local build and a release build.
//
// The parse in build.zig is deliberately dumb: keep this one line in the shape
// `const bitVersion: string = "..."` and keep it the only such line in the file.
const bitVersion: string = "0.1.0-dev"
